# Pairs with RAllOrNothing, and reproduces issue #4448 on the receiver. The
# point read path answers Indeterminate for a delegation whose coordinator
# cannot be dialled, but the snapshot read paths (SnapshotAsync,
# SnapshotWithRevisionAsync) leave such a txid out of the snapshot, and
# TxDecisionView resolves an absent txid to InFlight. A multi-key receiver
# reader resolving through a snapshot therefore serves a delegated tree's key
# pre-saga while the barrier has committed and a sibling tree is finalised.
# This edits the read view, not an action: it is the answer one class of
# reader is given, which is exactly where the defect lives.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingSnapshotReadsUnresolvableAsInFlight
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: an undiallable receiver delegation reads InFlight rather than Indeterminate, as the snapshot read paths answer it (#4448)

--- FIND
    ELSE IF rdeleg[tr] THEN (IF rdial[tr] THEN "indeterminate" ELSE cdec)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the unresolvable delegation is left out, so it reads InFlight.
    ELSE IF rdeleg[tr] THEN (IF rdial[tr] THEN "inflight" ELSE cdec)
--- END
